implement executable awareness for io.open_code

From: Skye Soss <skye@soss.website>

Add _Py_CheckExecFd() and _Py_CheckExecInteractive(), which call
execveat() with AT_EXECVE_CHECK and consult the securebits.

PEP 578 made io.open_code() the way to open a file whose contents will be
executed. Its default implementation now checks the opened file, and
raises PermissionError if the check fails and SECBIT_EXEC_RESTRICT_FILE is
set. This covers imported source and bytecode files, zipimport archives,
-m, runpy.run_path(), .pth files, and the scripts run by pdb, profile,
cProfile and trace. An open_code hook installed by an embedder with
PyFile_SetOpenCodeHook() replaces the default implementation, and with it
the check.

Bytecode caches now keep the execute bits of their source file, so a
module whose source is executable can still be imported from its cache.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
